{
  "info": {
    "name": "LIMS — Attachments",
    "description": "Attachment endpoints (Module 00).\n\nRoutes:\n  POST   /api/attachments                    (ADMIN/MANAGER)\n  GET    /api/attachments/:attachmentID      (any authenticated)\n  DELETE /api/attachments/:attachmentID      (ADMIN/MANAGER)\n\nFlow: Run 'Login as admin' first to seed {{accessToken}}. POST seeds {{attachmentID}}.\n\nUploads: multipart/form-data, single field `file`. Server validates MIME (image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp) and size (max 500 KB).\n\nReplace semantics: hard delete. When an owning entity (e.g. User) flips its FK, the controller hard-deletes the prior attachment in the same transaction. The DELETE endpoint here is for orphan cleanup or admin tooling.\n\nSee docs/modules/00-attachments.md and docs/decisions/ADR-attachments-storage-strategy.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl",       "value": "http://localhost:3033/api", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail",    "value": "admin@lims.local",          "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "Admin123",                  "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken",   "value": "",                          "type": "string" },
    { "key": "attachmentID",  "value": "",                          "type": "string" }
  ],
  "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const path = pm.request.url.getPath();",
          "const isLogin = /\\/auth\\/login$/.test(path);",
          "const isMultipart = (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'formdata');",
          "if (!isMultipart) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Content-Type', value: 'application/json' });",
          "}",
          "if (!isLogin) {",
          "  const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
          "  if (token) pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login as admin (seeds {{accessToken}})",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const res = pm.response.json();",
              "if (res?.data?.accessToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', res.data.accessToken);",
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Upload attachment (image, multipart) → seeds {{attachmentID}}",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "description": "Pick a JPG/PNG/WEBP image, max 500 KB"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/attachments",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["attachments"]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const res = pm.response.json();",
              "if (res?.data?.attachmentID) pm.collectionVariables.set('attachmentID', res.data.attachmentID);",
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('returns dataUrl', () => pm.expect(res.data.dataUrl).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get attachment by ID",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/attachments/{{attachmentID}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["attachments", "{{attachmentID}}"]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Delete attachment (hard delete)",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/attachments/{{attachmentID}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["attachments", "{{attachmentID}}"]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
